## Part 2 — Code to add to `pdf-stack-actions` (TypeScript)

Pseudocode-level per repo convention — substitute generated API names (`saNewDev…`) on paste. `canonicalize`, `sha256`, `uuid`, `nowIso` come from the existing `util.ts`.

### 2.1 `src/specBuilders/onePagerSpec.ts` — the shared builder (R1–R5 live here)

```typescript
export const ONE_PAGER_SPEC_VERSION = "1.0";

// THE single source of spec truth for workload 'one_pager'.
// Returns an OBJECT (never a string) + the stable retention key.
export async function buildOnePagerSpec(project: PlcProject): Promise<{
  spec: object;
  logicalReportKey: string;      // stable per subject — retention keeps latest N per key
}> {
  const onePagerText = project.onePagerText ?? "";
  const spec = {
    type: "one_pager",                        // == useCase == workload (WS-HARNESS §8 contract)
    specVersion: ONE_PAGER_SPEC_VERSION,
    projectId: project.projectId,
    title: project.displayName ?? project.projectId,
    asOfDate: isoDate(project.lastUpdatedAt), // YYYY-MM-DD — helper, not locale formatting
    content: {
      onePagerText,                           // the content payload — THIS is what makes
      status: project.status ?? "",           // specHash a content hash (data change => new hash)
    },
  };
  return { spec, logicalReportKey: `one_pager_${project.projectId}` };
}
```

### 2.2 `src/dedupCore.ts` — one decision function, both actions call it (R3 lives here)

```typescript
// NOT registered as an action — internal shared core.
// mode 'user':      HIT => DuplicateGeneratedReport copy for the requester (existing §1.3 behavior)
// mode 'scheduled': HIT => zero edits (a scheduled run that finds the render does NOTHING)
// Both modes:       error-status match or MISS => create pending ReportRequest
export async function dedupCore(
  useCase: string, spec: object, logicalReportKey: string,
  mode: "user" | "scheduled", userId: string | null,
): Promise<{ outcome: "hit_reused" | "hit_skipped" | "created"; specHash: string }> {
  const specJson = canonicalize(spec);                 // the ONLY stringification point
  const specHash = sha256(specJson);

  const existing = await Objects.GeneratedReport
    .where({ specHash, status: "complete" }).first();

  if (existing) {
    if (mode === "scheduled") return { outcome: "hit_skipped", specHash };
    // user path: hand the requester their own row via the copy action (WS-PDF §1.3 / KB §02 [Q2])
    await duplicateGeneratedReport(existing, uuid(), useCase, specHash);
    return { outcome: "hit_reused", specHash };
  }

  const r = Edits.create.ReportRequest(uuid());        // MISS (or only error-status matches)
  r.useCase = useCase; r.specJson = specJson; r.specHash = specHash;
  r.logicalReportKey = logicalReportKey;
  r.status = "pending"; r.trigger = mode === "scheduled" ? "scheduled" : "manual";
  r.requestedBy = userId; r.requestedAt = nowIso(); r.lastStatusChangeAt = nowIso();
  return { outcome: "created", specHash };
}
```

(Refactor note: the existing `SubmitReportRequestWithDedup` becomes a thin caller of this core with `mode:'user'` — one code path, no drift.)

### 2.3 `src/submitOnePagerReport.ts` — the user-facing wrapper action

```typescript
@OntologyEditFunction()   // register as action "[SA New Dev] Submit One Pager Report"
export async function submitOnePagerReport(project: PlcProject, userId: string): Promise<void> {
  const { spec, logicalReportKey } = await buildOnePagerSpec(project);   // R1: the shared builder
  await dedupCore("one_pager", spec, logicalReportKey, "user", userId);
}
```

Workshop's PDF button fires THIS action with the project object + current-user variable. The overlay then reads state off the request/report rows exactly as WS-PDF §4 already specifies — no frontend change beyond pointing the button at the wrapper.

### 2.4 `src/runScheduledPdfPregenOnePager.ts` — the Automate entry point

```typescript
@OntologyEditFunction()   // register as action "[SA New Dev] Run Scheduled Pdf Pregen One Pager"
export async function runScheduledPdfPregenOnePager(): Promise<void> {
  const projects = await Objects.PlcProject.where({ status: "active" }).all();  // standing subjects
  for (const p of projects) {
    try {
      const { spec, logicalReportKey } = await buildOnePagerSpec(p);   // SAME builder — R1
      await dedupCore("one_pager", spec, logicalReportKey, "scheduled", null);
    } catch (e) { /* skip subject whose spec can't build — never throw (batch must finish) */ }
  }
}
```

Unchanged subjects → `hit_skipped` → zero edits. If ALL subjects are unchanged, the `ReportRequest` dataset never updates and **no render build starts at all** — the free-run property.

