## Part 4 — Acceptance canary (run after first setup and after ANY builder change)

1. Fire the pregen action manually (action tester). Expect: one `pending` `ReportRequest` per active subject (`trigger='scheduled'`), the render build starts, PDFs reach `complete`.
2. Fire it again immediately. Expect: **zero new rows** and **no build starts** (all `hit_skipped`).
3. In Workshop, click the PDF button for any subject. Expect: **instant** — `hit_reused` (a duplicated report row for the user), overlay renders the PDF with **no loadscreen**, zero new renders.
4. Change one project's one-pager data. Re-fire pregen. Expect: exactly **one** new request/render (that subject), all others skipped.
5. Force one render to fail (bad payload). Next pregen run: expect that subject **resubmitted** (error-status match = MISS) — the self-heal property.

If step 3 shows a loadscreen instead of an instant hit, the two paths are not hashing identically — go straight to R3/R4 (nine times out of ten: array ordering, rounding, or a date formatted two ways).
